<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>FlatBars truthiness — edges &amp; Handlebars parity</title>
<style>
  body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 60rem; color: #1a1a1a; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: .4rem .6rem; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #f3f3f3; }
  code { background: #f3f3f3; padding: 0 .25rem; border-radius: 3px; }
  .t { color: #137333; font-weight: 600; }
  .f { color: #a50e0e; font-weight: 600; }
  .ok { color: #137333; }
  .bad { color: #a50e0e; font-weight: 600; }
  .note { background: #fff8e1; border-left: 4px solid #f9a825; padding: .6rem 1rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>FlatBars truthiness</h1>
<p>The <b>FlatBars</b> column is computed live by the engine
(<code>\{{#if v}}truthy\{{else}}falsy\{{/if}}</code>). The <b>Handlebars</b> column
is what Handlebars.js would decide for the same value. Rows marked
<span class="bad">✗</span> diverge.</p>

<table>
<thead>
  <tr><th>Value</th><th>FlatBars</th><th>Handlebars</th><th>Parity</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
  <tr>
    <td><code>false</code></td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "vFalse")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="f">falsy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>true</code></td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "vTrue")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>null</code></td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "vNull")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="f">falsy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>""</code> (empty string)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "sEmpty")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="f">falsy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>"hi"</code> (non-empty string)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "sText")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>"0"</code> (string zero)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "sZero")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>" "</code> (single space)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "sSpace")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>0</code> (number zero)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "nZero")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="f">falsy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>0</code> with <code>includeZero</code></td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "nZero") (dict "includeZero" true)}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span> (<code>includeZero=true</code>)</td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>42</code> (non-zero number)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "nNum")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>[]</code> (empty array)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "arrEmpty")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="f">falsy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>[1, 2]</code> (non-empty array)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "arrFull")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>{}</code> (empty object)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "objEmpty")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>{"k": 1}</code> (non-empty object)</td>
    <td>{{#if (lookup this "objFull")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>(safe "")</code> (empty trusted string)</td>
    <td>{{#if (safe "")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span> (a <code>SafeString</code> is an object)</td>
    <td><span class="bad">✗ differs</span></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><code>(safe "x")</code> (non-empty trusted string)</td>
    <td>{{#if (safe "x")}}<span class="t">truthy</span>{{else}}<span class="f">falsy</span>{{/if}}</td>
    <td><span class="t">truthy</span></td>
    <td><span class="ok">✓</span></td>
  </tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<p class="note">
<b>Parity with one edge.</b> FlatBars matches Handlebars' truthiness: the falsy
set is <code>false</code>, <code>null</code>, <code>0</code>, <code>""</code>, and
the empty array; everything else — including <code>{}</code> and non-zero numbers
— is truthy. Like Handlebars, <code>0</code> is falsy by default and counts as
truthy only with <code>includeZero</code> (passed as an options object:
<code>\{{#if n (dict "includeZero" true)}}…\{{/if}}</code>). The one remaining
difference is deliberate: marking a string safe never changes its truthiness —
a safe string tests as its <em>content</em>, so <code>safe ""</code> is
<b>falsy</b>, whereas a Handlebars <code>SafeString</code> is a truthy object.
Because <code>safe</code>/<code>esc_html</code> stringify first, <code>(safe
0)</code> is truthy while <code>0</code> is falsy — so testing an escaped/safe
value is a category error, and the validator warns about it.
</p>
</body>
</html>
